## Overview

The user approved the Paper & crimson preview and explicitly requested applying it to the current website on 14 October 2026. This edition shares warm paper surfaces, crimson navigation and a light/dark preference across the homepage, documentation, exact records, Craft, runtime pages, event and linked essays. Preserve product meaning, content, destinations and the adopted editorial voice.

## Colors

`source/governance-lab-series/assets/paper-crimson/appearance.css` owns documentation appearance roles. `palette.css` supplies the matching homepage roles. Keep concept and status hues distinct from navigation accents. Embedded SVG geometry and supplied raster artwork retain their original meaning. Dark diagram and role-map tints preserve each category while making selected labels readable.

## Typography

Use the approved Roboto Mono, SFMono-Regular, Cascadia Code, Liberation Mono, Consolas, monospace fallback stack. This is an explicit user-approved typography choice. The existing site typography remains a foundation; the appearance stylesheet supplies the adopted reading and navigation sizes. Keep reference contracts, code and diagram metrics readable without altering their text or geometry. Homepage supporting labels have a 12px floor.

## Layout

The centered knot and company-brain opening lead to a concrete incident example, session continuity, Craft and documentation destinations. The existing event announcement remains visible. The complete original homepage is retained in a native background disclosure; old fragment URLs reveal their original content.

Documentation retains its desktop tree, reading column and local outline, with native compact navigation. Start here adds six task-based reading paths and keeps its original introduction and quick links. Cards indicate a choice of destination; prose, contracts, comparison tables, graphs and catalog disclosures remain reading surfaces. Card grids stack when two readable columns do not fit.

## Elevation and Shapes

Use thin rules, restrained surfaces and 3px corners. Shadows clarify overlays rather than every content group. Preserve the logo, supplied imagery and SVG node/edge geometry. Wide diagrams expose visible scroll instructions, full-size links and keyboard scrolling.

## Components and Ownership

`paper_crimson.py` applies the maintained edition within the normal staged build. `reading_paths.py` owns path content/rendering; `diagram_presentation.py` owns the reviewed diagram affordances and map label wrapping. The paper-crimson asset folder contains shared appearance, theme/reading behavior and the approved vectors. Existing article, reference, runtime, event and graph renderers retain their content responsibilities.

Global search includes current runtime documentation and reading paths. Complete local payloads and plaintext fallback remain supported. Reading progress is browser-local and describes a reader's own notes. Event controls continue to distinguish phase, configured destinations and ballot readiness.

## Preservation and Verification

Preserve every existing route, fragment, paragraph, source link, formal record body, runtime article, code example and selected source file. Keep original homepage content discoverable through its disclosure and deep links. Do not replace newer current content with an older preview copy. Build from maintained source; do not hand-edit delivered HTML or deploy as a build side effect.

The previous visual context is retained with the local promotion evidence. This approval supersedes its distinct blue documentation, green essay and orb-hero presentation rules; their underlying content and assets remain available.
